**Theorem 4.7 (death-trim estimates for a fixed ordered epimorphism injection).** Let $A$ and $B$ be arbitrary finite positive-length interval families over an arbitrary field. Fix decreasing-death enumerations in each birth fiber and an occurrence injection $j:B\hookrightarrow A$ preserving birth and fiber ordinal, with $d_b\le d_{j(b)}$. Let $e:I_A\to I_B$ be an actual componentwise surjective natural map. For every $\eta\ge0$ satisfying $\ker e_t\subseteq\ker(I_A(t\to t+\eta))$ at every real $t$, the finite death of $j(b)$ is at most the finite death of $b$ plus $\eta$ whenever both are finite. More generally the finite-death trim of $j(b)$ is at most $d_b$, with infinite deaths left infinite. Every $A$ occurrence with $b+\eta<d$, including every essential, is in the range of the same fixed $j$. Paired essential deaths are equivalent. If $\eta=0$, $j$ is surjective and paired deaths agree.

